findings.citation_text:
750.510 - Employee observed washing hands without use of proper technique. Handle to paper towel dispenser was touched to retrieve paper towels after handwashing process was completed. Proper handwashing was discussed.

Employees shall properly wash their hands any time hands may have become contaminated and prior to handling food or clean equipment.
Procedure: Get paper towels ready...
1. rinse hands under clean running water;
2. apply soap;
3. rub hands together vigorously for at least 20 seconds;
4. thoroughly rinse hands under clean running water; 
5. dry hands (paper towels).
Use paper towels as a barrier to shut off manual faucet and/or the handle of paper towel dispenser (if more paper towels are needed)
